From 62225ca500c77a69962add8d3144efe9881522f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 02:17:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] transports+configstore: tenant-scoped budgets + rate limits
 CRUD (batched)

Completes the per-tenant admin surface over all governance metadata
entities. Mirrors the team / customer pattern: delegate-then-verify
with tenant_id re-pinning on PUT to defend against migration via
malicious payload.

Routes:
  POST   /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/budgets
  GET    /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/budgets
  GET    /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/budgets/{budget_id}
  PUT    /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/budgets/{budget_id}
  DELETE /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/budgets/{budget_id}

  POST   /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/rate-limits
  GET    /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/rate-limits
  GET    /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/rate-limits/{rate_limit_id}
  PUT    /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/rate-limits/{rate_limit_id}
  DELETE /api/tenants/{tid}/governance/rate-limits/{rate_limit_id}

configstore additions for both entities:
- *ByTenant list, *ForTenant single-get with cross-tenant ErrNotFound.
- *ForTenant Create/Update/Delete with the delegate-then-verify shape;
  Update re-pins tenant_id.
- MockConfigStore stubs (single-implementation delegation).
- Tests cover full CRUD across two tenants + cross-tenant isolation
  on each operation.

Transport additions:
- handlers.TenantBudgetsHandler with full CRUD. POST validates
  max_limit >= 0 and reset_duration via configstoreTables.ParseDuration.
  PUT accepts optional max_limit / reset_duration; empty patch -> 400.
- handlers.TenantRateLimitsHandler with full CRUD. POST requires at
  least one of token_max_limit / request_max_limit. PUT accepts any
  combination of the four fields; empty patch -> 400.
- Wires into server.go alongside the other tenant-scoped handlers.
- 12 handler tests covering happy paths, validation rejections,
  list filtering, cross-tenant GET/DELETE 404s, nil-store rejection.

Per-tenant admin surface is now complete for all entities (tenants,
providers, provider keys, virtual keys, MCP clients, teams,
customers, budgets, rate limits) with POST/GET-list/GET-single/PUT/
DELETE on each (provider keys use POST+DELETE for rotation).

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
